---
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";
import DataCard from "./DataCard.astro";
---

<div class="how-its-built" id="how-its-built">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section-inner">
			<SectionHeading
				title="How I Built This Portfolio"
				number={2}
				caption="Design tooling is so wild nowadays."
			/>
			<div class="data-cards">
				<DataCard
					number={1}
					title="Built a Database"
					tags={["Claude", "Notion"]}
				>
					<p>
						I had Claude create a database in Notion that distilled takeaways
						from NN/g articles and research papers.
					</p>
				</DataCard>
				<DataCard
					number={2}
					title="UX and UI"
					tags={["Claude", "Claude Design", "Windsurf"]}
				>
					<p>
						I had Claude reference the database to guide it while building
						wireframes and mock ups. I, also, fed it images of Japanese
						notebooks to build an aesthetic.
					</p>
				</DataCard>
				<DataCard
					number={3}
					title="Design Execution"
					tags={["Claude", "Figma"]}
				>
					<p>
						I had Claude push the the UI elements into Figma as a design system,
						and made manual adjustments.
					</p>
				</DataCard>
				<DataCard
					number={4}
					title="Spousal Privileges"
					tags={["My Wonderful Amazing Beautiful Talented Spouse"]}
				>
					<p>Instead of vibe coding, I worked with my developer spouse.</p>
				</DataCard>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.how-its-built {
		background-color: var(--black-umber);
		color: var(--crystal-cut);
	}

	.section-inner {
		padding-top: var(--space-20);
		padding-bottom: var(--space-20);
	}
	.data-cards {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: var(--space-6);
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
	}
</style>
